@cmbrose Noticed one issue.

`gh cs delete --repo cli/cli` deletes all codespaces without the flag `--all`

But the implementation of `--repo-owner` is slightly different, it expects the flag `--all` else it will show the choice page after filtering by repo owner. Should we make `--repo-owner` also behave like `--repo`?

comments:
@cmbrose Sorry for the confusion, but don't think `--owner` would be an ideal flag name here. In github's term any codespace that I create the owner would be me.
For example,
If I create codespace both in `cli/cli` and `kousikmitra/cli` both will have `kousikmitra` as owner.

```
"codespaces": [
    {
      "name": "xyz",
      "created_at": "2023-04-20T22:33:20+05:30",
      "display_name": "opulent space doodle",
      "last_used_at": "2023-04-20T22:33:20+05:30",
      "owner": {
        "login": "kousikmitra",
        "type": "User"
      },
      "repository": {
        "id": 123,
        "full_name": "cli/cli",
        "default_branch": ""
      },
      "state": "Available",
      ....
  },
  {
      "name": "abc",
      "created_at": "2023-04-20T22:46:16+05:30",
      "display_name": "automatic space xylophone",
      "last_used_at": "2023-04-20T22:46:16+05:30",
      "owner": {
        "login": "kousikmitra",
        "type": "User"
      },
      "repository": {
        "id": 789,
        "full_name": "kousikmitra/cli",
        "default_branch": ""
      },
      "state": "Provisioning",
      ...
   }
]
```

Now using `gh cs delete --owner kousikmitra` to delete codespaces related `kousikmitra/*` would be misleading.

Let me know your thoughts or if I am missing something here.
